{
  "id": "rock-and-roll-twelve-bars",
  "title": "Rock 'n' roll twelve bars",
  "cues": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "anchor": {
        "segment": 0,
        "offset": 0.2
      },
      "kind": "intro",
      "text": "In Carl Perkins's account, he wrote Blue Suede Shoes after hearing a dancer warn his date off his suede shoes.",
      "image": "artist-Q310339",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Blue Suede Shoes (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Suede_Shoes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "holly-arrives",
      "anchor": {
        "segment": 1,
        "offset": 2.1
      },
      "kind": "changeover",
      "text": "Buddy Holly's Peggy Sue now rides Perkins's band. Holly turned to rock and roll after seeing and opening for Elvis Presley in nineteen fifty-five.",
      "image": "artist-Q5977",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Peggy Sue (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peggy_Sue"
        },
        {
          "title": "Buddy Holly (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddy_Holly"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "charles-arrives",
      "anchor": {
        "segment": 3,
        "offset": 2.1
      },
      "kind": "changeover",
      "text": "Ray Charles now sings over Holly's band. He improvised What'd I Say to fill the end of a show.",
      "image": "artist-Q544387",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "What'd I Say (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What%27d_I_Say"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "twelve-bars",
      "anchor": {
        "segment": 3,
        "offset": 11.3
      },
      "kind": "song",
      "text": "It sets gospel call and response inside the twelve-bar form: four bars home, two on the four chord, two home, then five, four, and home.",
      "image": "artist-Q544387",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "What'd I Say (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What%27d_I_Say"
        },
        {
          "title": "Twelve-bar blues (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twelve-bar_blues"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dion-arrives",
      "anchor": {
        "segment": 5,
        "offset": 2.1
      },
      "kind": "changeover",
      "text": "Dion's The Wanderer now meets Charles's band. Ernie Maresca built it on a twelve-bar verse.",
      "image": "artist-Q1226921",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "The Wanderer (Dion song) (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wanderer_(Dion_song)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "outro",
      "anchor": {
        "segment": 6,
        "offset": 0.3
      },
      "kind": "outro",
      "text": "Dion loved Hank Williams, blues and doo-wop. One form carries all four.",
      "image": "artist-Q1226921",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Dion DiMucci (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dion_DiMucci"
        },
        {
          "title": "Twelve-bar blues (Wikipedia)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twelve-bar_blues"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
